Description: A domain-neutral framework for the analysis and visualisation
    of discrete-event, agent-based and node-actor simulation outputs. It
    serves as a general-purpose toolkit for systems in which entities
    (actors, nodes, agents) move through states and interact within
    spatial or network environments. Two output schemas (Profile A and
    Profile B) are supported through a common loader and profile-specific
    analysis functions, covering time-to-event analysis, policy and group
    comparisons, compliance and wait-gap indices, supply-demand ratios and
    sensitivity screening. An interactive 'shiny' dashboard and helpers for
    publication-ready figures and 'LaTeX' tables are included.
